course: dictionary
lesson: 8897
title: Shroud: a cover that hides
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shroud can be a cloth, and it can also mean anything that covers something up. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «Muslims usually bury their dead within a day, wrapped in a simple white cloth called a shroud.» The words wrapped in a simple white cloth tell you a shroud is the cloth around a body.
explain: Shroud can also be a doing word. «Fog shrouded the town.» Try the swap check: put covered in place of shrouded, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Fog covered the town, so shrouded means covered or hidden.
explain: The word also works in a picture sense. A shroud of mist is a thick layer of mist that hides things, and shrouded in mystery means hidden and secret. Clues like mist and mystery are the context that unlocks the meaning.
fact: A shroud is a cloth that a dead body is wrapped in before burial.
fact: «Shroud» can also mean something that covers or hides, such as a shroud of mist.
fact: As a verb, «shroud» means to cover or hide something: «Fog shrouded the town.»
fact: In sailing, a shroud is one of the ropes that hold a ship's mast steady.
fact: Useful phrases: shrouded in mist, shrouded in mystery, a shroud of secrecy.
exercise: «Muslims usually bury their dead within a day, wrapped in a simple white cloth called a shroud.» What is a shroud in this sentence? | *A cloth a dead body is wrapped in | A type of white bread | A kind of ship's rope | A wooden coffin
exercise: «Fog shrouded the town.» What does shrouded mean? | Washed clean by rain | Made very bright and sunny | *Covered or hidden | Built up with new houses
exercise: The old village was shrouded in mystery. Which word is closest in meaning to shrouded? | Lit | Cheerful | *Hidden | Painted
test: The crew checked each shroud on the mast before they sailed. What is a shroud on a ship? | A sailor's hat | A sail made of cloth | A small wooden boat | *A rope that holds the mast steady
test: «A shroud of secrecy hung over the plan.» What does shroud of secrecy suggest? | *A thick cover of hidden secrets | A happy party | A cold, wet blanket | Something openly shown to everyone
exam: Using the swap check, which word best replaces shroud in «a shroud of mist»? | Sunshine | Breeze | *Covering | Tower
